{"id": 1519, "stem": "<div class=\"relative w-full min-w-0 max-w-full self-stretch\" id=\"question-text\"><span><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><mark class=\"bg-transparent dark:text-neutral-100\" data-markjs=\"true\" style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">T</mark>he combined compliance of the lung and chest wall of a healthy individual is measured and plotted as shown below.\u00a0 It is noted that the intrapleural pressure at the end of maximal inspiration is -8 cm H<sub style=\"font-size: 1rem;\">2</sub>0 (marked x).</p><div class=\"mb-4 text-start flex justify-start items-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\"><div class=\"group/triggerable\" data-is-open=\"false\"><div class=\"group/draggable\" data-is-draggable=\"true\" data-is-dragging=\"false\"><div class=\"group/resizable relative\" data-is-maximized=\"false\" data-is-resizable=\"true\" data-is-resizing=\"false\"><div class=\"w-full\"><button class=\"lg:max-w-lg md:max-w-md w-fit max-w-full my-5 hover:scale-[1.01] transition-[transform,_box-shadow] ease-in-out duration-500 hover:shadow-lg\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"max-w-full h-auto rounded-none\" src=\"../../Assets/images/iuta4ua780ld7l7nhywa5yeo.jpg\"/></button></div></div></div></div></div><p class=\"mb-4 text-start\" style=\"margin-bottom: 1rem; font-weight: 400; font-size: 1rem;\">Which of the following is the best estimate of the intrapleural pressure at the point marked by the black dot?\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200c\u200b\u200b\u200c\u200b\u200b